infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Lazy vs eager: two defaults, both wrong as a standing default
  desc Declare relations plainly and load them explicitly per query instead
  compares
    - label Lazy relations
      children
        - label Promise-typed property
          desc Every await fires a fresh SELECT
        - label Hidden N+1 generator
          desc 100-author loop becomes 101 queries
        - label Under-fetches, then back-fills
          desc Cost invisible; reads like a property access
    - label Eager relations
      children
        - label Always joined on every find
          desc Every find(Author) drags posts over the wire
        - label Cannot opt out per query
          desc Count, name lookup, existence check all pay
        - label Over-fetches everywhere
          desc Cost hidden on the entity, not the call site
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b
